          "title": "Obtain joint measurability from actual iterates",
          "text": "Start every iteration at zero. Actual measurable eta/y and the continuous id-gradient map make every parameterized iterate measurable. Banach convergence and measurable limit prove measurability of the actual selector, rather than assuming a measurable choice.",
          "formula": "p_s=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}T_s^n(0),\\quad s\\mapsto p_s\\text{ measurable}.",
          "lean": "ContractingWith.fixedPoint; tendsto_iterate_fixedPoint; measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable"
        },
